        <briefdescription>
<para>Regenerates a manifest&apos;s declared outputs. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Parses and validates <computeroutput>manifestFile</computeroutput>, then processes every declared <computeroutput>## outputs</computeroutput> row (or only the row matching <computeroutput>outputFilter</computeroutput>, when given) in two passes: a validate-everything pass with no writes, then an identical pass that writes each output write-if-different (SPEC §8 atomicity — no output is written while any output could still fail validation).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>manifestFile</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>CAST.md</computeroutput> manifest to run. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>outputFilter</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>When non-empty, restricts regeneration to the named output row. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
